SLSKD:
I think it's probably safe to have gluetun mount a read only script to more
robustly modify slskd's config. Still don't really want to mess with the
gluetun control server, seems like that's difficult (and a potential security
vuln).

LVM:
Just want a simple role to create the LVM cache and scratch drives in /mnt/nas and /mnt/scratch.
Easiest to hardcode the disk UUIDs for this.

Containers:
- Separate wireguard VPN for port forwarding for transmission
  - I've moved transmission over, but haven't setup port forwarding from gluetun yet.
- Add auth for transmission (container supports a USER and PASSWORD field)
- tinymediamanager and syncthing should get moved to an entirely separate repo
  - I don't think there's any significant code duplication here, so probably
    don't need a shared task

Nicotine:
I might want to migrate this to nicotine.
https://hub.docker.com/r/sirjmann92/nicotineplus-proper
- This image just updated with experimental clipboard support with
  sirjmann92/nicotineplus-proper:test, which seems to be working reasonably
  well.
I think it's worth it to switch to this, or most likely run this in parallel
with slskd (m2m2r?). Port forwarding will still be a bit tricky - looks like
the container has curl thankfully, so I can query the gluetun control server
and maybe set an environment variable.

Tailscale:
Tailscale grants are currently being used to control who has access to what on
the tailnet. I like this system - it's good enough that we can skip using
firewalld for the most part and just trust tailscale.

Tailscale grants are setup as json. I want a system where each system on the
tailnet specifies its own json for who can access it.
